## Known limitations

- Every container gets `10.0.0.2/24`, so only one container can run at a time.
- `/dev` is not populated, so containers have no `/dev/null`, `/dev/urandom`, etc.
- The outgoing interface is hardcoded to `wlan0` (`OUT_IFACE`).
- Only one `/etc/subuid` / `/etc/subgid` line per user is supported. With multiple lines, the
  parsed start and count contain several values and `unshare` fails.
- No cgroup namespace, so `/sys/fs/cgroup` inside the container doesn't show its own limits
  (they are still enforced).
- The rootfs URL and architecture are hardcoded to Alpine 3.19.1 x86_64.
- Host setup requires `sudo`; the bridge, NAT rule and parent cgroup persist until `uninstall`.